<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for a hardened-runtime macOS build.

  Inert today: no Developer ID certificate exists for this project, so nothing
  is signed and nothing is notarised. They are committed anyway because the
  hardened runtime is declared in `package.json`, and because adding a
  certificate later should be a secrets change rather than a code change.

  Each one is here for a reason, and there are only three:

  * JIT and unsigned executable memory are what V8 needs. Electron does not
    start under a hardened runtime without them.
  * `disable-library-validation` is required because the app runs a *downloaded*
    `llama-server` and its dylibs. They are fetched at first use, digest-checked
    against a pinned manifest, and signed by nobody - so library validation
    would refuse to load them.

  Deliberately absent: camera, microphone, address book, and every network
  server entitlement. The gateway binds loopback by itself and the sandbox
  entitlement is not requested at all, so none of them would be doing anything.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
